<!--
  MCU multicast-session-rx buffer-pool config (Round B) — the SSOT for the
  lwIP (MCU / bare-metal) host's MULTICAST session-link receive slot-pool
  dimensions (RFC 5.K buffer_pools block; session-fsm 3.1 multicast
  transport rx).

  Sibling of session_rx_pool_mcu.scxml (the UNICAST session-rx pool). It is
  a DISTINCT pool, not a reuse, because the multicast transport socket is a
  separate long-lived runtime instance from the unicast session socket: a
  node can run both at once (one unicast session + one multicast group), so
  each owns its own rx-queue and is sized independently. SCE codegen emits
  the SLOT_COUNT / SLOT_SIZE constants the MCU link tier consumes as the
  const-generic parameters of the multicast session receive socket —
  wz-link-lwip::rx_sockets::SessionMulticastRxSocket =
  LwipUdpSocket&lt;SLOT_SIZE, SLOT_COUNT&gt;. SLOT_COUNT sizes the
  callback-to-application heapless::spsc::Queue depth (Q); SLOT_SIZE sizes
  the per-datagram payload capacity (N).

  Values:
    - slot_count 32  — TWICE the unicast pool's 16. The unicast session rx
      sees one peer; the multicast transport aggregates Join / Frame /
      KeepAlive from up to N group members arriving in the same cooperative
      tick (the 3.1 RxDispatch fan-in), so the rx-queue needs more burst
      headroom before the recv copy drains it. 32 is the full-rate
      (AP-class) headroom; a constrained-MCU slim multicast profile (the
      multicast analogue of session_rx_pool_mcu_minimal) is a deploy
      follow-up, not authored until a slim multicast deploy needs it.
    - slot_size 1536 — cache-line multiple; &gt;= udp_session.mtu_bytes
      (1472), so a full-MTU multicast data frame fits without truncation
      (identical to the unicast session pool — the wire frame is the same
      shape on either transport).

  cache-policy is none here (NOT the deploy.yaml mcu_node's maintain), for
  the same reason as session_rx_pool_mcu.scxml: the live consumer
  (LwipUdpSocket) copies each datagram via pbuf_copy_partial into an inline
  heapless::Vec, not the 5.E DMA slot table, so it performs no DMA cache
  maintenance. The eventual isr_to_pool DMA-staged multicast rx path is a
  separate, not-yet-wired concern; the two pool dims this emit feeds the
  socket are identical under either policy.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       sce:kind="buffer-pool" name="session_rx_pool_mcu_multicast" version="1.0">
  <sce:slot-count>32</sce:slot-count>
  <sce:slot-size>1536</sce:slot-size>
  <sce:section>sram1</sce:section>
  <sce:alignment>32</sce:alignment>
  <sce:cache-policy>none</sce:cache-policy>
</scxml>
